# interplay_lifetime_heap_alias_buffers: Two buffers placed in one private heap over the same range (types 13 and 14: A at offset 0 and B at offset 0x4000, each two pages, so A's second page is B's first). Both read the guest bytes the heap was paged from; a fill through A shows through B in the next exec, and a fill through B through A. In-process the heap is a host copy (a legacy placement heap paged by one blit): the guest pages keep their bytes until an exec lists the heap with invalidateGuest and synchronize (6), which writes both fills back. In the service the heap is a detach heap over the guest pages: each fill is in the guest pages at once.
